{
  "_doc": "Maier et al. 2018 (Nature 555:623-628, PMID 29555994): the 1,197-drug x 40-strain growth screen, read from the Europe PMC supplementary tables for PMC6108420. Every cell of the matrix was measured, so this fragment declares TWO relationships and not one: INHIBITS_GROWTH_OF for the 5,592 hits and DOES_NOT_INHIBIT_GROWTH_OF for the 42,233 measured non-hits, which is the population no other source in this graph has for drugs and the reason D8 can be asked in the negative. Two types rather than a flag is Part D's own rule for this layer (ALTERS_TAXON / ALTERS_SUBSTANCE, never one) and NJC19's for the exchange layer. Drug is declared here as well as in chembl.json because this source mints nodes for the 437 catalogue entries no ChEMBL join route reaches, keyed on the Prestwick number; the four screen_* / prestwick_* columns are empty on ChEMBL's own rows, which is what the merge in microbiomekg.tables is for.",
